    "result": "I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 68 tests covering spec examples, malformed input, and round trips. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (68 passed). `encode` groups runs with `itertools.groupby`, writes runs of four or more as `~n~c`, and doubles `~` for shorter runs. `decode` scans left to right, handling `~~`, `~count~c` and plain characters, and raises `ValueError` for a trailing `~`, a non-digit after `~`, a count with leading zeros, a count below 4, a count not followed by `~`, or a missing character. One test failed on my first run because I had written the wrong expected value for `\"abbbbc\"`; I corrected the expectation to `\"a~4~bc\"` and the suite then passed. I kept the given signatures, edited only `solution.py` and `tests/`, and installed nothing.",
